# CODEOWNERS file for Tikka
# This file defines who is automatically requested for review based on the
# files changed in a pull request.
#
# Format: <file-pattern> <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Owners can be GitHub usernames (@username) or teams (@org/team-name).
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# TWO RULES THAT ARE EASY TO GET WRONG, AND HAVE BEEN GOT WRONG HERE BEFORE:
#
#   1. The LAST matching pattern wins — it does not accumulate. A later `*`
#      line silently replaces every owner assigned above it. Keep the broad
#      patterns at the top and the narrow ones at the bottom, and never repeat
#      a pattern.
#   2. An owner that does not exist, or that lacks write access, makes the
#      whole line invalid and assigns NO reviewer. GitHub reports this under
#      Settings -> Branches, and the file previously named a `@maintainers`
#      team that the org never had, so nothing was ever assigned. Before
#      adding a team here, confirm it exists in the `crackedstudio` org and
#      has write access to this repository.
#
# CODEOWNERS only requests review. It is enforced only once branch protection
# on `master` has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled — see SECURITY.md.

